    "created_at": "2019-02-25T15:24:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-02-25T15:24:49Z",
    "body": "Well, it's meaningless on operations that are non-callback-interface operations, because it affects JS-to-IDL conversions, and those happen for return values of callback operations but not the other ones.  So allowing it on non-callback operations makes no sense at all.\r\n\r\nFor dictionaries, the argument for not allowing it is that it's not used there now, and its a legacy feature we don't want to proliferate, so it would be better to not allow it places where it's not used.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
